#: src/help.h:8
#, c-format
msgid ""
"\n"
" \n"
" \n"
"                                   XFE, X File Explorer File Manager\n"
" \n"
"                                     <http://roland65.free.fr/xfe>\n"
"                                 <http://sourceforge.net/projects/xfe>\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"  This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it "
"under the terms of the GNU\n"
"  General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation; "
"either version 2, or (at your option)\n"
"  any later version.\n"
" \n"
"  This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but "
"WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; \n"
"  without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A "
"PARTICULAR PURPOSE. \n"
"  See the GNU General Public License for more details.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Description\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  X File Explorer (Xfe) is a lightweight file manager for X11, written using "
"the FOX toolkit.\n"
"  It is desktop independent and can easily be customized.\n"
"  It has Commander or Explorer styles and is very fast and small.\n"
"  Xfe is based on X Win Commander, written by Maxim Baranov.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Features\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"     - Very fast graphic user interface\n"
"     - Small memory footprint\n"
"     - UTF-8 support\n"
"     - HiDPI monitor support\n"
"     - Commander/Explorer interface with four file manager modes : a) one "
"panel, b) a folder tree\n"
"       and one panel, c) two panels and d) a folder tree and two panels\n"
"     - Horizontal or vertical file panels stacking\n"
"     - Dockable toolbars\n"
"     - Panels synchronization and switching\n"
"     - Tabs\n"
"     - Places panel with customizable bookmarks\n"
"     - Optional expandable folders in detailed file lists\n"
"     - Per-folder .hidden files to hide named files and folders\n"
"     - Customizable columns in detailed file list mode\n"
"     - Integrated text editor and viewer (X File Write, Xfw)\n"
"     - Integrated image viewer (X File Image, Xfi)\n"
"     - Integrated archive viewer and extractor (X File Archive, Xfa)\n"
"     - Integrated package (rpm or deb) viewer / installer / uninstaller (X "
"File Package, Xfp)\n"
"     - Custom shell scripts (like Nautilus scripts)\n"
"     - Mount/Unmount devices with optional automounter (Linux only, supports "
"MTP devices)\n"
"     - Managing network shares (Windows shares or connecting to SSH server)\n"
"     - Search files and directories\n"
"     - Bulk rename files\n"
"     - Optional natural sort order (foo10.txt comes after foo2.txt...)\n"
"     - Copy/Cut/Paste files from and to your favorite desktop (GNOME/KDE/"
"XFCE)\n"
"     - Drag and Drop files from and to your favorite desktop (GNOME/KDE/"
"XFCE)\n"
"     - Disk usage command \n"
"     - Root mode with authentication by pkexec, sudo or su\n"
"     - File associations\n"
"     - Optional trash can for file delete operations (compliant with "
"freedesktop.org standards)\n"
"     - Double click or single click file and folder navigation\n"
"     - Mouse right click pop-up menu in tree list and file list\n"
"     - Change file attributes\n"
"     - Customizable color themes (GNOME, KDE, XFCE, Dark, ...)\n"
"     - Warn when mount point are not responding (Linux only)\n"
"     - Back and forward history lists for folder navigation\n"
"     - Customizable color themes (GNOME, KDE, XFCE, Dark, ...)\n"
"     - Icon themes (Default, GNOME, KDE, XFCE, ...)\n"
"     - Create archives (tar, zip, gzip, bzip2, xz, zst, 7z, ...)\n"
"     - Extract archives (many formats are supported)\n"
"     - File / folder comparison (through external tool, ex: meld)\n"
"     - Tooltips with file properties\n"
"     - Progress bars or dialogs for lengthy file operations\n"
"     - Thumbnails image previews\n"
"     - Configurable key bindings\n"
"     - Startup notification (optional)\n"
"     - and much more...\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Default Key bindings\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Below are the global default key bindings. These key bindings are common "
"to all X File applications.\n"
" \n"
"     * Select all                         - Ctrl-A\n"
"     * Copy to clipboard                  - Ctrl-C\n"
"     * Search                             - Ctrl-F\n"
"     * Search previous                    - Ctrl-Shift-G\n"
"     * Search next                        - Ctrl-G\n"
"     * Go to home folder                  - Ctrl-H\n"
"     * Invert selection                   - Ctrl-I\n"
"     * Open file                          - Ctrl-O\n"
"     * Print file                         - Ctrl-P\n"
"     * Quit application                   - Ctrl-Q\n"
"     * Paste from clipboard               - Ctrl-V\n"
"     * Close window                       - Ctrl-W\n"
"     * Cut to clipboard                   - Ctrl-X\n"
"     * Deselect all                       - Ctrl-Z\n"
"     * Display help                       - F1\n"
"     * Create new file                    - Ctrl-N\n"
"     * Create new folder                  - F7\n"
"     * Big icon list                      - F10\n"
"     * Small icon list                    - F11\n"
"     * Detailed file list                 - F12\n"
"     * Toggle display hidden files        - Ctrl-F6\n"
"     * Toggle display thumbnails          - Ctrl-F7\n"
"     * Vertical panels                    - Ctrl-Shift-F1\n"
"     * Horizontal panels                  - Ctrl-Shift-F2\n"
"     * Go to working folder               - Shift-F2\n"
"     * Go to parent folder                - Backspace\n"
"     * Go to previous folder              - Ctrl-Backspace\n"
"     * Go to next folder                  - Shift-Backspace\n"
" \n"
" \n"
"  Below are the default X File Explorer key bindings. These key bindings are "
"specific to the Xfe application.\n"
" \n"
"     * Add bookmark                      - Ctrl-B\n"
"     * Filter files                      - Ctrl-D\n"
"     * Execute command                   - Ctrl-E\n"
"     * Create new symbolic link          - Ctrl-J\n"
"     * Switch panels                     - Ctrl-K\n"
"     * Clear address bar                 - Ctrl-L\n"
"     * Mount file system (Linux only)    - Ctrl-M\n"
"     * Rename files                      - F2\n"
"     * Refresh panels                    - Ctrl-R\n"
"     * Symlink files to location         - Ctrl-S\n"
"     * Launch terminal                   - Ctrl-T\n"
"     * Unmount file system (Linux only)  - Ctrl-U\n"
"     * Synchronize panels                - Ctrl-Y\n"
"     * Create new window                 - F3\n"
"     * Edit                              - F4\n"
"     * Copy files to location            - F5\n"
"     * Move files to location            - F6\n"
"     * File properties                   - F9\n"
"     * One panel mode                    - Ctrl-F1\n"
"     * Tree and panel mode               - Ctrl-F2\n"
"     * Two panels mode                   - Ctrl-F3\n"
"     * Tree and two panels mode          - Ctrl-F4\n"
"     * Toggle display hidden folders     - Ctrl-F5\n"
"     * Go to trash can                   - Ctrl-F8\n"
"     * Create new root window            - Shift-F3\n"
"     * View                              - Shift-F4\n"
"     * Move files to trash can           - Del\n"
"     * Restore files from trash can      - Alt-Del\n"
"     * Delete files                      - Shift-Del\n"
"     * Copy file names to clipboard      - Ctrl-Shift-N\n"
"     * Empty trash can                   - Ctrl-Del\n"
"     * New Tab                           - Shift-F1\n"
"     * Connect to Server                 - Shift-F5\n"
" \n"
" \n"
"  Below are the default X File Image key bindings. These key bindings are "
"specific to the Xfi application.\n"
" \n"
"     * View previous image               - Ctrl-J\n"
"     * View next image                   - Ctrl-K\n"
"     * Zoom to fit window                - Ctrl-F\n"
"     * Zoom to fit window                - Ctrl-F\n"
"     * Mirror image horizontally         - Ctrl-H\n"
"     * Zoom image to 100%                - Ctrl-I\n"
"     * Rotate image to left              - Ctrl-L\n"
"     * Rotate image to right             - Ctrl-R\n"
"     * Mirror image vertically           - Ctrl-V\n"
" \n"
" \n"
"  Below are the default X File Write key bindings. These key bindings are "
"specific to the Xfw application.\n"
" \n"
"     * Toggle word wrap mode             - Ctrl-K\n"
"     * Goto line                         - Ctrl-L\n"
"     * Create new document               - Ctrl-N\n"
"     * Replace string                    - Ctrl-R\n"
"     * Save changes to file              - Ctrl-S\n"
"     * Toggle line numbers mode          - Ctrl-T\n"
"     * Toggle upper case mode            - Ctrl-Shift-U\n"
"     * Toggle lower case mode            - Ctrl-U\n"
"     * Redo last change                  - Ctrl-Y\n"
"     * Undo last change                  - Ctrl-Z\n"
" \n"
" \n"
"  X File Archive (Xfa) and X File Package (Xfp) only use some of the global "
"key bindings.\n"
" \n"
"  Note that all the default key bindings listed above can be customized in "
"the Xfe Preferences dialog. However,\n"
"  some key actions are hardcoded an cannot be changed. These include:\n"
" \n"
"     * Ctrl-+ and Ctrl--                 - zoom in and zoom out image in "
"Xfi\n"
"     * Ctrl-Shift-F10                    - display context menus in Xfe\n"
"     * Space                             - select an item in file list\n"
"     * Return                            - enter folders in file lists, open "
"files, select button actions, etc.\n"
"     * Esc                               - close current dialog, unselect "
"files, etc.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Drag and Drop operations\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Dragging a file or group or files (by moving the mouse while maintaining "
"the left button pressed)\n"
"  to a folder or a file panel optionally opens a dialog that allows you to "
"select the file operation: copy,\n"
"  move, link or cancel.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Trash system\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Xfe implements a trash system that is fully compliant with the "
"freedesktop.org standards.\n"
"  This allows you to move files to the trash can and to restore files from "
"within Xfe or your favorite desktop.\n"
"  Note that the trash files location is: ~/.local/share/Trash/files\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Configuration\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  You can perform any Xfe customization (layout, file associations, key "
"bindings, etc.) without editing any file\n"
"  by hand. However, you may want to understand the configuration principles, "
"because some customizations can also\n"
"  easily be done by manually editing the configurations files.\n"
"  Be careful to quit Xfe before manually editing any configuration file, "
"otherwise changes could not be taken\n"
"  into account.\n"
" \n"
"  The system-wide configuration file xferc is located in /usr/share/xfe, /"
"usr/local/share/xfe\n"
"  or /opt/local/share/xfe, in the given order of precedence.\n"
" \n"
"  The local configuration files for Xfe, Xfw, Xfi, Xfa and Xfp are now "
"located in the ~/.config/xfe folder.\n"
"  They are named xferc, xfwrc, xfirc, xfarc and xfprc.\n"
"  \n"
"  At the very first Xfe run, the system-wide configuration file is copied "
"into the local configuration file\n"
"  ~/.config/xfe/xferc which does not exists yet. If the system-wide "
"configuration file is not found\n"
"  (in case of an unusual install place), a dialog asks the user to select "
"the right place. It is thus easier to\n"
"  customize Xfe (this is particularly true for the file associations) by "
"hand editing because all the local options\n"
"  are located in the same file.\n"
" \n"
"  Default PNG icons are located in /usr/share/xfe/icons/default-theme or /"
"usr/local/share/xfe/icons/default-theme,\n"
"  depending on your installation. You can easily change the icon theme path "
"in the Preferences dialog.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   HiDPI support\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Starting with version 1.44, Xfe supports HiDPI monitors. All users have to "
"do is to manually adjust the screen\n"
"  resolution using the Edit / Preferences / Appearance / DPI option. A value "
"of 200 - 240 dpi should be fine for Ultra\n"
"  HD (4K) monitors.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Dockable Toolbars\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Starting with version 2.1, toolbars can be docked to the four corners of "
"the window and their positions are saved\n"
"  (Xfe only) if the Auto save layout option is enabled in Edit Preferences / "
"General dialog. To dock a toolbar, \n"
"  left click on its handle and drag it to the destination corner, or right "
"click on it and use the popup menu.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Places\n"
"   =-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Starting with version 2.0, the folder panel features two tabs: one is the "
"classic Tree view and the other\n"
"  is a Places view. This Places view allows you to view desktop folders "
"(home, downloads, documents, music, ...), of\n"
"  drive mounts, network shares and user's bookmarks.\n"
" \n"
"  Network shares mounted from the desktop using gvfs (GNOME or XFCE) appear "
"in the Places view and can be unmounted\n"
"  (KDE network shares are not supported). Mount points for removable devices "
"also appear in the Places view.\n"
" \n"
"  Bookmarks can be added, removed and customized (order, name and icon) "
"using a context menu.\n"
" \n"
"  The Places view is optional as is also the Tree view (related settings are "
"located in the\n"
"  Preferences / General dialog).\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Tabs\n"
"   =-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Starting with version 2.1, it is possible to add tabs by pressing Shift-F1 "
"or by clicking on the + icon of the tab\n"
"  toolbar. A right click on a tab displays a popup menu that offers to move "
"a tab or close it.\n"
" \n"
"  The tab toolbar can be always shown or hidden if not used. Options related "
"to tabs usage can be found in the\n"
"  Edit / Preferences / Settings dialog.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Scripts\n"
"   =-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Custom shell scripts can be executed from within Xfe on the files that are "
"selected in a panel. You have to first\n"
"  select the files you want to proceed, then right click on the file list "
"and go to the Scripts sub menu. Last, choose\n"
"  the script you want to apply on the selected files.\n"
" \n"
"  The script files must be located in the ~/.config/xfe/scripts folder and "
"have to be executable. You can organize\n"
"  this folder as you like by using sub-folders. You can use the Tools / Go "
"to script folder menu item to directly go\n"
"  to the script folder and manage it.\n"
" \n"
"  Here is an example of a simple shell script that list each selected file "
"on the terminal from where Xfe was\n"
"  launched:\n"
" \n"
"  #!/bin/sh\n"
"  for arg\n"
"  do\n"
"  /bin/ls -la \"$arg\"\n"
"  done\n"
" \n"
"  You can of course use programs like xmessage, zenity or kdialog to display "
"a window with buttons that allows you to\n"
"  interact with the script. Here is a modification of the above example that "
"uses xmessage:\n"
" \n"
"  #!/bin/sh\n"
"  (\n"
"  echo  \"ls -la\"\n"
"  for arg\n"
"  do\n"
"  /bin/ls -la \"$arg\"\n"
"  done\n"
"  ) | xmessage -file -\n"
" \n"
"  Most often, it is possible to directly use Nautilus scripts found on the "
"Internet without modifications.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Search files and directories\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Xfe can quickly search files and directories by using find and grep "
"command backends. This is done through the\n"
"  Tools / Search files menu item (or by using the Ctrl-F shortcut).\n"
" \n"
"  In the search window, users can then specify usual search patterns like "
"name and text, but more sophisticated search\n"
"  options are also available (size, date, permissions, users, groups, follow "
"symlinks and empty files). Results appear\n"
"  in a file list and users can use the right click menu to manage their "
"files, the same way as they do in the file\n"
"  panels.\n"
" \n"
"  The search can be interrupted by clicking on the Stop button or pressing "
"the Escape key.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Bulk rename files\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Xfe can perform a bulk rename operation on selected files and folders from "
"the file panels. The rename dialog allows\n"
"  you to replace a text pattern or insert / overwrite / remove text at a "
"given position. It is also possible to number\n"
"  files.\n"
" \n"
"  Bulk rename can also be used from the search panel results. However, in "
"that case it is not possible to rename\n"
"  folders to avoid moving file locations.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Non Latin based languages\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Xfe can display its user interface and also the file names in non latin "
"character based languages, provided that you\n"
"  have selected a Unicode font that supports your character set. To select a "
"suitable font, use the\n"
"  Edit / Preferences / Font menu item.\n"
" \n"
"  Multilingual Unicode TrueType fonts can be found at this address: "
"http:    //www.slovo.info/unifonts.htm\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Automounting\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Starting with version 2.1, Xfe has an integrated automounter program that "
"allows you to mount removable disks\n"
"  or media when they are inserted. The automounter also supports MTP devices "
"(ex: Android phones or tablets).\n"
" \n"
"  The automounter is optional and should only be used if your system does "
"not already provides that feature. By\n"
"  default, it is disabled and can be enabled in the Edit / Preferences / "
"Settings dialog.\n"
" \n"
"  The automounter relies on udisks2 and gvfs / gio, so these components must "
"be installed on your system. The process\n"
"  is called xfe-automount and is launched when the session opens.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Network Shares\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Starting with version 2.1, it is possible to mount a Windows network share "
"or to connect to an SSH server\n"
"  (Linux only, gvfs / gio must be installed). For that, use the Tools / "
"Connect to Server menu item (Shift-F5\n"
"  shortcut) or use the Connect to Server toolbar icon. This will display a "
"dialog asking for your connection\n"
"  parameters.\n"
" \n"
"  It is possible to safely retain connection passwords provided that the "
"secret-tool utility is installed on your\n"
"  system. Note that in Debian based distributions this utility is provided "
"by the libsecret-tools package. In other\n"
"  distributions, it is usually included in the libsecret library.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Custom Color Themes\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Starting with version 2.1, it is possible to save the current theme to a "
"custom theme, that can be renamed\n"
"  or removed. You can thus have different custom color themes and easily "
"switch between them.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Tips\n"
"   =-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  File list\n"
"     - Select files and right click to open a context menu on the selected "
"files\n"
"     - Press Ctrl + right click to open a context menu on the file panel\n"
"     - When dragging a file/folder to a folder, hold on the mouse on the "
"folder to open it\n"
"     - Displayed colums and column order can be selected in the "
"Preferences / File List dialog\n"
" \n"
"  Tree list\n"
"     - Select a folder and right click to open a context menu on the "
"selected folder\n"
"     - Press Ctrl + right click to open a context menu on the tree panel\n"
"     - When dragging a file/folder to a folder, hold on the mouse on the "
"folder to expand it\n"
" \n"
"  Copy/paste file path or name\n"
"     - Select a file and press Ctrl-C to copy the file path to the "
"clipboard. Then in a dialog or an application,\n"
"       press Ctrl-V to paste the file path. Use the Copy name menu item (or "
"press Ctrl-Shift-N) to copy the file\n"
"       name (without path) to the clipboard. \n"
"     - In a file operation dialog, select a file name in the line containing "
"the source name and paste it directly\n"
"       to the destination using the middle button of your mouse. Then modify "
"it to suit your needs.\n"
" \n"
"  Add files to the clipboard\n"
"     - You can select files from a folder, copy them to the clipboard by "
"pressing Ctrl-C. This erases the previous\n"
"       clipboard content. Then, you can move to another folder, select other "
"files and add them to the clipboard\n"
"       content by pressing Ctrl-Shift-C. This does not erase the previous "
"clipboard content. At last, you can move\n"
"       to the destination and press Ctrl-V to copy all the files you have in "
"the clipboard. Of course, this also works\n"
"       with Ctrl-X and Ctrl-Shift-X to cut and paste the files.\n"
" \n"
"  File / folder comparison\n"
"     - In a file panel, select two files or two folders to compare them "
"(using the external comparator tool defined in\n"
"       Edit / Preferences / Programs) by right clicking and selecting the "
"Compare menu item.\n"
"     - In a file panel, select a file or folder to compare it with another "
"file or folder by right clicking and\n"
"       selecting the Compare menu item. Use the dialog to enter the name of "
"the file or folder to compare with,\n"
"       or click on the icon to browse and select an item.\n"
"     - In two panels mode or tree and two panel mode, select one file or one "
"folder per panel, then right click and\n"
"       select the Compare menu item to open the external comparator tool.\n"
" \n"
"  Startup notification\n"
"     - Startup notification is the process that displays a feedback (a "
"sandbox cursor or whatever) to the user when\n"
"       he has started an action (file copying, application launching, etc.). "
"Depending on the system, there can be\n"
"       some issues with startup notification. If Xfe was compiled with "
"startup notification support, the user can\n"
"       disable it for all applications at the global Preferences level. He "
"can also disable it for individual\n"
"       applications, by using the dedicated option in the first tab of the "
"Properties dialog. This latter way is\n"
"       only available when the file is an executable. Disabling startup "
"notification can be useful when starting\n"
"       an old application that doesn't support the startup notification "
"protocol (e.g. Xterm).\n"
" \n"
"   Root mode\n"
"     - If pkexec is installed and configured on your system, then this is "
"the best way to switch to root mode\n"
"     - If you use the sudo root mode, it can be useful to add password "
"feedback to the sudo command. For this purpose,\n"
"       edit your sudoers file like this:\n"
"           sudo visudo -f /etc/suoders\n"
"       and then add 'pwfeedback' to the default options, as shown below:\n"
"           Defaults         env_reset,pwfeedback\n"
"       After that, you should see stars (like *****) when you type your "
"password in the small authentication window.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Bugs\n"
"   =-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Please report any found bug to Roland Baudin <roland65@free.fr>. Don't "
"forget to mention the Xfe version you use,\n"
"  the FOX library version and your system name and version.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Translations\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
"  \n"
"  Xfe is now available in 25 languages but some translations are only "
"partial. To translate Xfe to your language,\n"
"  open the Xfe.pot file located in the po folder of the source tree with a "
"software like poedit, kbabel\n"
"  or gtranslator and fill it with your translated strings (be careful to the "
"hotkeys and c-format characters),\n"
"  and then send it back to me. I'll be pleased to integrate your work in the "
"next Xfe release.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Patches\n"
"   =-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  If you have coded some interesting patch, please send it to me, I will try "
"to include it in the next release...\n"
" \n"
"  Many thanks to Maxim Baranov for his excellent X Win Commander, to Jeroen "
"van der Zijp for the FOX toolkit\n"
"  and  to all people that have provided useful patches, translations, tests "
"and advices.\n"
" \n"
"  [Last revision: 11/11/2026]\n"
" \n"
" "
msgstr ""
"\n"
" \n"
" \n"
"                                   XFE, filhåndteringen X File Explorer\n"
" \n"
"                                     <http://roland65.free.fr/xfe>\n"
"                                 <http://sourceforge.net/projects/xfe>\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"  Dette program er fri software. Du må videredistribuere og ændre det under "
"betingelserne i GNU General\n"
"  Public License, som udgivet af Free Software Foundation, enten version 2 "
"af licensen eller, efter eget valg,\n"
"  en senere version.\n"
" \n"
"  Programmet distribueres i håb om, at det vil være nyttigt, men UDEN NOGEN "
"GARANTI;\n"
"  ikke engang den underforståede garanti om SALGBARHED eller EGNETHED TIL ET "
"BESTEMT FORMÅL.\n"
"  Se GNU General Public License for flere oplysninger.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Beskrivelse\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  X File Explorer (Xfe) er en let filhåndtering til X11, skrevet med FOX-"
"biblioteket.\n"
"  Det er uafhængigt af skrivebordsmiljøet og kan nemt tilpasses.\n"
"  Det tilbyder Commander- og Explorer-visninger og er meget hurtigt og "
"kompakt.\n"
"  Xfe er baseret på X Win Commander, skrevet af Maxim Baranov.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Funktioner\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"     - Meget hurtig grafisk brugerflade\n"
"     - Lavt hukommelsesforbrug\n"
"     - Understøttelse af UTF-8\n"
"     - Understøttelse af HiDPI-skærme\n"
"     - Commander/Explorer-brugerflade med fire tilstande: a) ét panel, b) et "
"mappetræ og ét panel,\n"
"       c) to paneler og d) et mappetræ og to paneler\n"
"     - Vandret eller lodret placering af filpaneler\n"
"     - Værktøjslinjer, der kan fastgøres\n"
"     - Synkronisering af og skift mellem paneler\n"
"     - Faner\n"
"     - Stedpanel med bogmærker, der kan tilpasses\n"
"     - Valgfrie mapper, der kan udfoldes i detaljerede fillister\n"
"     - .hidden-filer i hver mappe til at skjule filer og mapper efter navn\n"
"     - Kolonner, der kan tilpasses i detaljeret fillistevisning\n"
"     - Indbygget teksteditor og tekstviser (X File Write, Xfw)\n"
"     - Indbygget billedviser (X File Image, Xfi)\n"
"     - Indbygget arkivviser og arkivudpakning (X File Archive, Xfa)\n"
"     - Indbygget visning, installation og afinstallation af rpm- og deb-"
"pakker (X File Package, Xfp)\n"
"     - Brugerdefinerede shellscripts, ligesom Nautilus-scripts\n"
"     - Montering og afmontering med valgfri automatisk montering (kun Linux, "
"understøtter MTP-enheder)\n"
"     - Håndtering af netværksdelinger (Windows-delinger eller forbindelse "
"til SSH-servere)\n"
"     - Søgning efter filer og mapper\n"
"     - Masseomdøbning af filer\n"
"     - Valgfri naturlig sortering (foo10.txt kommer efter foo2.txt...)\n"
"     - Kopiering, klipning og indsættelse af filer fra og til dit foretrukne "
"skrivebord (GNOME/KDE/XFCE)\n"
"     - Træk og slip af filer fra og til dit foretrukne skrivebord (GNOME/KDE/"
"XFCE)\n"
"     - Kommando til visning af diskforbrug\n"
"     - Root-tilstand med godkendelse via pkexec, sudo eller su\n"
"     - Filtilknytninger\n"
"     - Valgfri papirkurv til sletning af filer, i overensstemmelse med "
"freedesktop.org-standarderne\n"
"     - Navigation i filer og mapper med dobbeltklik eller enkeltklik\n"
"     - Genvejsmenu med højreklik i træ- og fillister\n"
"     - Ændring af filegenskaber\n"
"     - Farvetemaer, der kan tilpasses (GNOME, KDE, XFCE, mørkt...)\n"
"     - Advarsler, når monteringspunkter ikke svarer (kun Linux)\n"
"     - Historik til at gå tilbage og frem under mappenavigation\n"
"     - Farvetemaer, der kan tilpasses (GNOME, KDE, XFCE, mørkt...)\n"
"     - Ikontemaer (standard, GNOME, KDE, XFCE...)\n"
"     - Oprettelse af arkiver (tar, zip, gzip, bzip2, xz, zst, 7z...)\n"
"     - Udpakning af arkiver i mange formater\n"
"     - Sammenligning af filer og mapper med et eksternt værktøj, f.eks. "
"meld\n"
"     - Værktøjstip med filegenskaber\n"
"     - Fremdriftslinjer eller dialoger ved langvarige filhandlinger\n"
"     - Forhåndsvisning af billeder som miniaturer\n"
"     - Tastaturgenveje, der kan tilpasses\n"
"     - Valgfri opstartsmeddelelse\n"
"     - Og meget mere...\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Standardtastaturgenveje\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Herunder vises de globale standardgenveje, der er fælles for alle X File-"
"programmer.\n"
" \n"
"     * Markér alle                      - Ctrl-A\n"
"     * Kopiér til udklipsholder          - Ctrl-C\n"
"     * Søg                              - Ctrl-F\n"
"     * Find forrige                     - Ctrl-Shift-G\n"
"     * Find næste                       - Ctrl-G\n"
"     * Gå til hjemmemappe               - Ctrl-H\n"
"     * Invertér markering               - Ctrl-I\n"
"     * Åbn fil                          - Ctrl-O\n"
"     * Udskriv fil                      - Ctrl-P\n"
"     * Afslut program                   - Ctrl-Q\n"
"     * Indsæt fra udklipsholder          - Ctrl-V\n"
"     * Luk vindue                       - Ctrl-W\n"
"     * Klip til udklipsholder            - Ctrl-X\n"
"     * Fjern alle markeringer           - Ctrl-Z\n"
"     * Vis hjælp                        - F1\n"
"     * Opret ny fil                     - Ctrl-N\n"
"     * Opret ny mappe                   - F7\n"
"     * Liste med store ikoner           - F10\n"
"     * Liste med små ikoner             - F11\n"
"     * Detaljeret filliste              - F12\n"
"     * Vis/skjul skjulte filer          - Ctrl-F6\n"
"     * Vis/skjul miniaturer             - Ctrl-F7\n"
"     * Lodrette paneler                 - Ctrl-Shift-F1\n"
"     * Vandrette paneler                - Ctrl-Shift-F2\n"
"     * Gå til arbejdsmappe              - Shift-F2\n"
"     * Gå til overordnet mappe          - Backspace\n"
"     * Gå til forrige mappe             - Ctrl-Backspace\n"
"     * Gå til næste mappe               - Shift-Backspace\n"
" \n"
" \n"
"  Herunder vises standardgenvejene, der kun gælder for X File Explorer "
"(Xfe).\n"
" \n"
"     * Tilføj bogmærke                  - Ctrl-B\n"
"     * Filtrér filer                    - Ctrl-D\n"
"     * Kør kommando                     - Ctrl-E\n"
"     * Opret ny symbolsk lænke          - Ctrl-J\n"
"     * Skift panel                      - Ctrl-K\n"
"     * Ryd adresselinje                 - Ctrl-L\n"
"     * Montér filsystem (kun Linux)     - Ctrl-M\n"
"     * Omdøb filer                      - F2\n"
"     * Opdatér paneler                  - Ctrl-R\n"
"     * Opret symbolske lænker på placering - Ctrl-S\n"
"     * Start terminal                   - Ctrl-T\n"
"     * Afmontér filsystem (kun Linux)   - Ctrl-U\n"
"     * Synkronisér paneler              - Ctrl-Y\n"
"     * Opret nyt vindue                 - F3\n"
"     * Redigér                          - F4\n"
"     * Kopiér filer til placering       - F5\n"
"     * Flyt filer til placering         - F6\n"
"     * Filegenskaber                    - F9\n"
"     * Tilstand med ét panel            - Ctrl-F1\n"
"     * Tilstand med træ og ét panel     - Ctrl-F2\n"
"     * Tilstand med to paneler          - Ctrl-F3\n"
"     * Tilstand med træ og to paneler   - Ctrl-F4\n"
"     * Vis/skjul skjulte mapper         - Ctrl-F5\n"
"     * Gå til papirkurven               - Ctrl-F8\n"
"     * Opret nyt root-vindue            - Shift-F3\n"
"     * Vis                              - Shift-F4\n"
"     * Flyt filer til papirkurven       - Del\n"
"     * Gendan filer fra papirkurven     - Alt-Del\n"
"     * Slet filer                       - Shift-Del\n"
"     * Kopiér filnavne til udklipsholder - Ctrl-Shift-N\n"
"     * Tøm papirkurven                  - Ctrl-Del\n"
"     * Ny fane                          - Shift-F1\n"
"     * Forbind til server               - Shift-F5\n"
" \n"
" \n"
"  Herunder vises standardgenvejene, der kun gælder for X File Image (Xfi).\n"
" \n"
"     * Vis forrige billede              - Ctrl-J\n"
"     * Vis næste billede                - Ctrl-K\n"
"     * Tilpas billedet til vinduet      - Ctrl-F\n"
"     * Tilpas billedet til vinduet      - Ctrl-F\n"
"     * Spejl billedet vandret           - Ctrl-H\n"
"     * Zoom billedet til 100%           - Ctrl-I\n"
"     * Drej billedet til venstre        - Ctrl-L\n"
"     * Drej billedet til højre          - Ctrl-R\n"
"     * Spejl billedet lodret            - Ctrl-V\n"
" \n"
" \n"
"  Herunder vises standardgenvejene, der kun gælder for X File Write (Xfw).\n"
" \n"
"     * Slå tekstombrydning til/fra      - Ctrl-K\n"
"     * Gå til linje                     - Ctrl-L\n"
"     * Opret nyt dokument               - Ctrl-N\n"
"     * Erstat tekst                     - Ctrl-R\n"
"     * Gem ændringer i fil              - Ctrl-S\n"
"     * Vis/skjul linjenumre             - Ctrl-T\n"
"     * Slå store bogstaver til/fra      - Ctrl-Shift-U\n"
"     * Slå små bogstaver til/fra        - Ctrl-U\n"
"     * Gentag sidste ændring            - Ctrl-Y\n"
"     * Fortryd sidste ændring           - Ctrl-Z\n"
" \n"
" \n"
"  X File Archive (Xfa) og X File Package (Xfp) bruger kun nogle af de "
"globale genveje.\n"
" \n"
"  Alle standardgenvejene ovenfor kan tilpasses i Xfes indstillinger. Nogle "
"tastaturhandlinger er dog\n"
"  fastlagt i programmet og kan ikke ændres. Det gælder blandt andet:\n"
" \n"
"     * Ctrl-+ og Ctrl--                 - zoom ind og ud på billedet i Xfi\n"
"     * Ctrl-Shift-F10                   - vis genvejsmenuer i Xfe\n"
"     * Mellemrum                        - markér et element i fillisten\n"
"     * Enter                            - åbn mapper og filer, aktivér "
"knapper osv.\n"
"     * Esc                              - luk den aktuelle dialog, fjern "
"markering af filer osv.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Træk og slip\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Når du trækker en fil eller en gruppe filer til en mappe eller et filpanel "
"ved at flytte musen,\n"
"  mens venstre knap holdes nede, kan der åbnes en dialog, hvor du vælger "
"handlingen: kopiér, flyt,\n"
"  opret lænke eller annullér.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Papirkurv\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Xfe har en papirkurv, som følger freedesktop.org-standarderne fuldt ud.\n"
"  Du kan flytte filer til papirkurven og gendanne dem fra Xfe eller dit "
"foretrukne skrivebord.\n"
"  Papirkurvens filer ligger i: ~/.local/share/Trash/files\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Konfiguration\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Du kan tilpasse Xfe (layout, filtilknytninger, tastaturgenveje osv.) uden "
"at redigere filer manuelt.\n"
"  Det kan dog være nyttigt at forstå principperne bag konfigurationen, da "
"nogle tilpasninger også nemt\n"
"  kan udføres ved at redigere konfigurationsfilerne i hånden.\n"
"  Afslut Xfe, før du redigerer en konfigurationsfil manuelt; ellers bliver "
"ændringerne muligvis ikke\n"
"  taget i brug.\n"
" \n"
"  Den globale konfigurationsfil xferc ligger i /usr/share/xfe, /usr/local/"
"share/xfe\n"
"  eller /opt/local/share/xfe, i den angivne prioritetsrækkefølge.\n"
" \n"
"  De lokale konfigurationsfiler til Xfe, Xfw, Xfi, Xfa og Xfp ligger i "
"mappen ~/.config/xfe.\n"
"  De hedder xferc, xfwrc, xfirc, xfarc og xfprc.\n"
"  \n"
"  Første gang Xfe startes, kopieres den globale konfigurationsfil til den "
"lokale konfigurationsfil\n"
"  ~/.config/xfe/xferc, som endnu ikke findes. Hvis den globale fil ikke "
"findes, f.eks. på grund af\n"
"  en usædvanlig installationsplacering, beder en dialog dig om at vælge den "
"rigtige placering.\n"
"  Det gør det nemmere at tilpasse Xfe manuelt, især filtilknytningerne, "
"fordi alle lokale indstillinger\n"
"  findes i samme fil.\n"
" \n"
"  Standardikonerne i PNG-format ligger i /usr/share/xfe/icons/default-theme "
"eller\n"
"  /usr/local/share/xfe/icons/default-theme, afhængigt af installationen. Du "
"kan nemt ændre stien\n"
"  til ikontemaet i indstillingerne.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   HiDPI-understøttelse\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Fra version 1.44 understøtter Xfe HiDPI-skærme. Du skal blot justere "
"skærmopløsningen manuelt under\n"
"  Redigér / Indstillinger / Udseende / DPI. En værdi på 200 - 240 dpi er "
"normalt passende til Ultra HD-skærme (4K).\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Værktøjslinjer, der kan fastgøres\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Fra version 2.1 kan værktøjslinjer fastgøres i vinduets fire hjørner. "
"Placeringerne gemmes (kun i Xfe),\n"
"  hvis automatisk lagring af layout er aktiveret under Redigér / "
"Indstillinger / Generelt.\n"
"  Fastgør en værktøjslinje ved at venstreklikke på dens håndtag og trække "
"den til det ønskede hjørne,\n"
"  eller højreklik på den og brug genvejsmenuen.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Steder\n"
"   =-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Fra version 2.0 har mappepanelet to faner: den klassiske trævisning og "
"visningen Steder.\n"
"  Steder viser skrivebordets mapper (hjem, hentninger, dokumenter, "
"musik...), monterede drev,\n"
"  netværksdelinger og brugerens bogmærker.\n"
" \n"
"  Netværksdelinger, der er monteret fra skrivebordet med gvfs (GNOME eller "
"XFCE), vises under Steder\n"
"  og kan afmonteres. KDE-netværksdelinger understøttes ikke. "
"Monteringspunkter for flytbare enheder\n"
"  vises også under Steder.\n"
" \n"
"  Bogmærker kan tilføjes, fjernes og tilpasses (rækkefølge, navn og ikon) "
"via en genvejsmenu.\n"
" \n"
"  Både Steder og trævisningen er valgfrie. De tilhørende indstillinger "
"findes under\n"
"  Indstillinger / Generelt.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Faner\n"
"   =-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Fra version 2.1 kan du tilføje faner ved at trykke på Shift-F1 eller "
"klikke på ikonet + i fanelinjen.\n"
"  Højreklik på en fane åbner en menu, hvor du kan flytte eller lukke fanen.\n"
" \n"
"  Fanelinjen kan altid vises eller skjules, når den ikke bruges. "
"Indstillinger for faner findes under\n"
"  Redigér / Indstillinger / Opsætning.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Scripts\n"
"   =-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Brugerdefinerede shellscripts kan køres fra Xfe på de filer, der er "
"markeret i et panel.\n"
"  Markér først de filer, du vil behandle, højreklik derefter på fillisten, "
"og åbn undermenuen Scripts.\n"
"  Vælg til sidst det script, du vil anvende på de markerede filer.\n"
" \n"
"  Scriptfilerne skal ligge i mappen ~/.config/xfe/scripts og være "
"eksekverbare. Du kan organisere\n"
"  denne mappe, som du vil, med undermapper. Brug Værktøjer / Gå til "
"scriptmappe for at gå direkte\n"
"  til scriptmappen og håndtere indholdet.\n"
" \n"
"  Her er et eksempel på et enkelt shellscript, som viser hver markeret fil i "
"den terminal,\n"
"  hvorfra Xfe blev startet:\n"
" \n"
"  #!/bin/sh\n"
"  for arg\n"
"  do\n"
"  /bin/ls -la \"$arg\"\n"
"  done\n"
" \n"
"  Du kan også bruge programmer som xmessage, zenity eller kdialog til at "
"vise et vindue med knapper,\n"
"  som gør det muligt at interagere med scriptet. Her er en ændret udgave af "
"eksemplet, der bruger xmessage:\n"
" \n"
"  #!/bin/sh\n"
"  (\n"
"  echo  \"ls -la\"\n"
"  for arg\n"
"  do\n"
"  /bin/ls -la \"$arg\"\n"
"  done\n"
"  ) | xmessage -file -\n"
" \n"
"  I de fleste tilfælde kan du bruge Nautilus-scripts fra internettet direkte "
"uden ændringer.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Søgning efter filer og mapper\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Xfe kan hurtigt søge efter filer og mapper ved hjælp af kommandoerne find "
"og grep.\n"
"  Brug Værktøjer / Søg efter filer eller genvejen Ctrl-F.\n"
" \n"
"  I søgevinduet kan du angive almindelige søgekriterier som navn og tekst, "
"men også mere avancerede\n"
"  indstillinger: størrelse, dato, rettigheder, brugere, grupper, symbolske "
"lænker og tomme filer.\n"
"  Resultaterne vises i en filliste, hvor du kan bruge genvejsmenuen til at "
"håndtere filerne,\n"
"  ligesom i filpanelerne.\n"
" \n"
"  Søgningen kan afbrydes ved at klikke på Stop eller trykke på Escape.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Masseomdøbning af filer\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Xfe kan omdøbe markerede filer og mapper i filpanelerne samlet. "
"Omdøbningsdialogen giver mulighed\n"
"  for at erstatte et tekstmønster eller indsætte, overskrive og fjerne tekst "
"på en bestemt position.\n"
"  Du kan også nummerere filerne.\n"
" \n"
"  Masseomdøbning kan også bruges på resultaterne i søgepanelet. Her kan "
"mapper dog ikke omdøbes,\n"
"  så filernes placeringer ikke ændres.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Sprog med ikke-latinske alfabeter\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Xfe kan vise brugerfladen og filnavne på sprog med ikke-latinske "
"alfabeter, hvis du har valgt\n"
"  en Unicode-skrifttype, der understøtter det nødvendige tegnsæt. Vælg en "
"passende skrifttype under\n"
"  Redigér / Indstillinger / Skrifttyper.\n"
" \n"
"  Flersprogede Unicode TrueType-skrifttyper findes på: http://www.slovo.info/"
"unifonts.htm\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Automatisk montering\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Fra version 2.1 indeholder Xfe et program til automatisk montering af "
"flytbare diske og medier,\n"
"  når de tilsluttes. Det understøtter også MTP-enheder, f.eks. Android-"
"telefoner og -tablets.\n"
" \n"
"  Automatisk montering er valgfri og bør kun bruges, hvis systemet ikke "
"allerede har denne funktion.\n"
"  Den er som standard deaktiveret og kan aktiveres under Redigér / "
"Indstillinger / Opsætning.\n"
" \n"
"  Programmet afhænger af udisks2 og gvfs / gio, som derfor skal være "
"installeret på systemet.\n"
"  Processen hedder xfe-automount og startes, når sessionen åbnes.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Netværksdelinger\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Fra version 2.1 kan du montere en Windows-netværksdeling eller forbinde "
"til en SSH-server\n"
"  (kun Linux, med gvfs / gio installeret). Brug Værktøjer / Forbind til "
"server, genvejen Shift-F5\n"
"  eller det tilsvarende ikon på værktøjslinjen. Der åbnes en dialog, som "
"beder om forbindelsesoplysninger.\n"
" \n"
"  Adgangskoder til forbindelser kan gemmes sikkert, hvis værktøjet secret-"
"tool er installeret.\n"
"  På Debian-baserede distributioner leveres det af pakken libsecret-tools. "
"På andre distributioner\n"
"  er det normalt en del af biblioteket libsecret.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Brugerdefinerede farvetemaer\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Fra version 2.1 kan du gemme det aktuelle tema som et brugerdefineret "
"tema, der kan omdøbes eller fjernes.\n"
"  Du kan dermed have flere brugerdefinerede farvetemaer og nemt skifte "
"mellem dem.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Tips\n"
"   =-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Filliste\n"
"     - Markér filer og højreklik for at åbne en genvejsmenu for de markerede "
"filer.\n"
"     - Hold Ctrl nede og højreklik for at åbne en genvejsmenu for "
"filpanelet.\n"
"     - Når du trækker en fil eller mappe til en mappe, skal du holde musen "
"over mappen for at åbne den.\n"
"     - De viste kolonner og deres rækkefølge vælges under Indstillinger / "
"Filliste.\n"
" \n"
"  Træliste\n"
"     - Markér en mappe og højreklik for at åbne dens genvejsmenu.\n"
"     - Hold Ctrl nede og højreklik for at åbne en genvejsmenu for "
"træpanelet.\n"
"     - Når du trækker en fil eller mappe til en mappe, skal du holde musen "
"over mappen for at udfolde den.\n"
" \n"
"  Kopiering og indsættelse af filsti eller filnavn\n"
"     - Markér en fil og tryk på Ctrl-C for at kopiere filstien til "
"udklipsholderen. Tryk derefter på Ctrl-V\n"
"       i en dialog eller et program for at indsætte stien. Brug Kopiér navn "
"eller Ctrl-Shift-N for kun\n"
"       at kopiere filnavnet uden sti.\n"
"     - I en dialog til filhandlinger kan du markere et filnavn i kildelinjen "
"og indsætte det direkte\n"
"       i destinationen med musens midterknap. Tilpas det derefter efter "
"behov.\n"
" \n"
"  Tilføj filer til udklipsholderen\n"
"     - Markér filer i en mappe og kopiér dem med Ctrl-C. Det erstatter "
"udklipsholderens tidligere indhold.\n"
"       Gå derefter til en anden mappe, markér flere filer, og tilføj dem med "
"Ctrl-Shift-C uden at slette\n"
"       det tidligere indhold. Gå til sidst til destinationen og tryk på Ctrl-"
"V for at kopiere alle filerne\n"
"       i udklipsholderen. Du kan også bruge Ctrl-X og Ctrl-Shift-X til at "
"klippe og indsætte filerne.\n"
" \n"
"  Sammenligning af filer og mapper\n"
"     - Markér to filer eller to mapper i et filpanel, højreklik, og vælg "
"Sammenlign for at åbne det eksterne\n"
"       sammenligningsprogram, som er angivet under Redigér / Indstillinger / "
"Programmer.\n"
"     - Hvis du vil sammenligne en fil eller mappe med en anden, skal du "
"markere den, højreklikke og vælge\n"
"       Sammenlign. Indtast navnet på den fil eller mappe, der skal "
"sammenlignes med, eller klik på ikonet\n"
"       for at finde og vælge et element.\n"
"     - I tilstanden med to paneler eller træ og to paneler skal du markere "
"én fil eller mappe i hvert panel,\n"
"       højreklikke og vælge Sammenlign for at åbne det eksterne "
"sammenligningsprogram.\n"
" \n"
"  Opstartsmeddelelse\n"
"     - En opstartsmeddelelse viser brugeren, at en handling er startet, "
"f.eks. filkopiering eller opstart\n"
"       af et program, med en ventemarkør eller en anden indikator. Der kan "
"være problemer afhængigt\n"
"       af systemet. Hvis Xfe er kompileret med denne funktion, kan den "
"deaktiveres for alle programmer\n"
"       i de generelle indstillinger. Den kan også deaktiveres for enkelte "
"programmer med indstillingen\n"
"       på den første fane i Egenskaber. Denne mulighed findes kun for "
"eksekverbare filer.\n"
"       Det kan være nyttigt at deaktivere funktionen for ældre programmer, "
"der ikke understøtter\n"
"       protokollen for opstartsmeddelelser, f.eks. Xterm.\n"
" \n"
"  Root-tilstand\n"
"     - Hvis pkexec er installeret og konfigureret, er det den bedste måde at "
"skifte til root-tilstand på.\n"
"     - Hvis du bruger root-tilstand med sudo, kan det være nyttigt at vise "
"feedback, når adgangskoden indtastes.\n"
"       Redigér filen sudoers på denne måde:\n"
"           sudo visudo -f /etc/suoders\n"
"       Tilføj derefter 'pwfeedback' til standardindstillingerne som vist "
"her:\n"
"           Defaults         env_reset,pwfeedback\n"
"       Du vil nu se stjerner (som *****) i det lille godkendelsesvindue, når "
"du indtaster adgangskoden.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Fejl\n"
"   =-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Indberet fejl til Roland Baudin <roland65@free.fr>. Husk at angive din Xfe-"
"version, versionen\n"
"  af FOX-biblioteket samt systemets navn og version.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Oversættelser\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=-=-=\n"
"  \n"
"  Xfe findes på 25 sprog, men nogle oversættelser er kun delvise. Hvis du "
"vil oversætte Xfe til dit sprog,\n"
"  skal du åbne filen Xfe.pot i kildetræets po-mappe med et program som "
"poedit, kbabel eller gtranslator\n"
"  og udfylde oversættelserne. Vær opmærksom på genvejstaster og C-"
"formattegn.\n"
"  Send derefter filen til mig; jeg vil med glæde medtage dit arbejde i næste "
"udgave af Xfe.\n"
" \n"
" \n"
" \n"
"   Rettelser\n"
"   =-=-=-=-=\n"
" \n"
"  Hvis du har skrevet en interessant rettelse, så send den til mig. Jeg vil "
"forsøge at medtage den i næste udgave...\n"
" \n"
"  Mange tak til Maxim Baranov for det fremragende X Win Commander, til "
"Jeroen van der Zijp for FOX-biblioteket\n"
"  og til alle, der har bidraget med rettelser, oversættelser, tests og gode "
"råd.\n"
" \n"
"  [Senest revideret: 11/11/2026]\n"
" \n"
" "

#: src/main.cpp:325
msgid ""
"\n"
"Usage: xfe [options...] [FOLDER|FILE...]\n"
"\n"
"    [options...] are the following:\n"
"\n"
"        -h,   --help         Print (this) help screen and exit.\n"
"        -v,   --version      Print version information and exit.\n"
"        -i,   --iconic       Start iconified.\n"
"        -m,   --maximized    Start maximized.\n"
"        -p n, --panel n      Force panel view mode to n (n=0 => Tree and one "
"panel,\n"
"                             n=1 => One panel, n=2 => Two panels, n=3 => "
"Tree and two panels).\n"
"\n"
"    [FOLDER|FILE...] is a list of folders or files to open on startup.\n"
"    The first two folders are displayed in the file panels, the others are "
"ignored.\n"
"    The number of files to open is not limited.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"Brug: xfe [valg...] [MAPPE|FIL...]\n"
"\n"
"    [valg...] er følgende:\n"
"\n"
"        -h,   --help         Vis (denne) hjælpetekst og afslut.\n"
"        -v,   --version      Vis versionsoplysninger og afslut.\n"
"        -i,   --iconic       Start minimeret.\n"
"        -m,   --maximized    Start maksimeret.\n"
"        -p n, --panel n      Sæt panelvisningen til n (n=0 => Træ og ét "
"panel,\n"
"                             n=1 => Ét panel, n=2 => To paneler, n=3 => Træ "
"og to paneler).\n"
"\n"
"    [MAPPE|FIL...] er en liste over mapper eller filer, der skal åbnes ved "
"opstart.\n"
"    De første to mapper vises i filpanelerne; resten ignoreres.\n"
"    Antallet af filer, der kan åbnes, er ubegrænset.\n"
"\n"

